sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1 (record-only update starts no run), R2-R4, 5 (swamp role SSH identity), round 2 bugs (refuse with no server, server admin password by its own vault key, cleanup on pass or fail).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: database:update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>services-valkey
  CLI->>GW: database:update cache<br/>--database=3
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit database:update cache --database=3`
  %%> - syntax: `<slug> [--driver=DRIVER] [--node=NODE] [--host=HOST] [--port=PORT] [--database=NAME] [--path=PATH] [--username=USER] [--password=SECRET] [--idempotency-key=KEY]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the connection slug, and at least one field to replace
  %%> - `--node=` with an empty value clears the Node association
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - the keys already stored on attached Instances; run `instance:database:add` again, then `env:sync`
  Note over GW: Validate the change<br/>connection cache · Valkey index
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the fields fit the driver (`validation.failed`)
  %%> - a managed connection keeps its identity and credentials (`database.server_connection_managed`); on a Valkey server only the index may change
  %%> - an attached Instance stays on the same Node as the connection
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - a change that needs a live check runs on its Database server's Node only: today, a new index on a managed Valkey server
  %%> - every other change is record-only
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a change that needs a live check on a connection without a Database server (`database.server_required`)
  %%> - a run never targets the Gateway Node
  alt record-only change
    Note over GW: Write the change<br/>R1: no run · DatabaseUpdated
    %%> When:
    %%> - any change that needs no live check, for example a new password on a registered external database
    %%> Result:
    %%> - connection `cache` is updated, its password encrypted
    %%> - no task and no Swamp run start (R1); nothing changes on any Node
    GW-->>CLI: 200 Updated<br/>connection cache
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the updated record at once; there is nothing to follow
  else new index on a Valkey server
    Note over GW: Hold the change<br/>task #5122 · lock services-valkey
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the change is recorded in task #5122; connection `cache` keeps its current values
    %%> - no other change runs on `services-valkey`; the Gateway holds one lock per Database server
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>…-database-connection-update
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts one Swamp run of `operation-database-connection-update` on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the requested index 3, and the server's WireGuard address and port
    %%> - the vault key name `database-server-5-admin`; the admin password itself never enters the intent
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5122
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Copy the action scripts<br/>@swamp/ssh copy · /tmp/…-5122
    %%> How:
    %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior
    %%> - the SSH identity is the one the `swamp` role owns, at its one role-defined place
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - copies the shipped script into `/tmp/orbit-database-update-5122`
    SW->>N: Check the index fits<br/>CONFIG GET databases
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the live server's database count and checks that index 3 is below it
    %%> How:
    %%> - the step reads the admin password with `vault.get` and passes it on standard input
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - no write on the server; the index is a client setting
    SW->>N: Remove the scripts<br/>always runs · rm -rf /tmp/…-5122
    %%> When:
    %%> - always, after the check, whether it passed or failed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes `/tmp/orbit-database-update-5122`, so no scripts stay on Node 12
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the task result does not change; the directory holds no secrets
    alt index fits
      N-->>SW: 16 databases
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the server's database count; index 3 fits
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Apply the change<br/>index 3 · task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - connection `cache` records index 3
      %%> - task #5122 succeeds
    else index too high or check fails
      N--xSW: out of range or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - index 3 is not below the server's count, or SSH or the Valkey login fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code, for example `validation.failed`
      Note over GW: Keep the connection<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - connection `cache` keeps its old index
      %%> - task #5122 fails, with the change it held
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - nothing changed; the check only reads
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the command again with a valid index; it is a new task
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5122
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
